The original version is part of the match, so a stale write matches nothing:

```csharp
if (!db.Orders.TryGetValue(id, out var row) || row.Version != originalVersion)
    throw new DbUpdateConcurrencyException("... affected 0 row(s).");
db.Orders[id] = new Row(status, row.Version + 1);
return row.Version + 1;
```

`PutOrder` answers 404 first, then maps the exception to 409 with the current version. The tests catch the plausible wrong version that matches on the id alone (last writer wins): the stale-version test sees the row overwritten and the two-edits test sees 200 twice, which is exactly the lost update the token exists to stop. A version that maps the conflict to 404 or lets the exception escape as a 500 fails the 409 tests.

